 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+The session lives in the member's cookie ([keep sessions in signed cookies](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md)).
+`sign` in `larder/sessions.py` writes the member id and the expiry as JSON, base64-encoded, followed by `.` and its
+HMAC-SHA256 under the key; `verify` returns the member, or `None` when the signature does not match or the expiry has
+passed. Every web server reads the key from `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`, kept in the deploy secrets; a server without it
+falls back to the key `dev-only`, so a server deployed without the secret accepts cookies anyone can forge and
+rejects those the other servers sign.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- **No server-side logout of one member.** A session ends only when its expiry passes, up to 30 minutes after the
+  last request. Workaround: none short of rotating the key, which logs out everyone.
+- **Rotating the key logs out every member.** Workaround: rotate `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` only between pickups, on every
+  server at once.
 
